  "id": "DrugBank_DB00137 - MONDO_6733",
  "verbalization": "Lutein is implicated in the pathogenesis of Dry Eye Syndrome through a series of indirect pathways involving Xerophthalmia and polyethylene glycol derivatives. The evidence suggests that Lutein is associated with Xerophthalmia, a condition that is itself linked to Dry Eye Syndrome via multiple routes. Specifically, Lutein is connected to Lifitegrast and Polyethylene Glycol 3500, both of which are indicated to cause Dry Eye Syndrome. The overlapping connections between Lutein and Xerophthalmia, along with the shared indication to Dry Eye Syndrome, indicate a potential mechanism where Lutein may influence the development of Dry Eye Syndrome through the indirect effects of these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Lutein in modulating the physiological processes that contribute to Dry Eye Syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
